)<small>the quiet village of Oakhaven, there lived an old watchmaker named Elias who could fix any clock, but never his own. His shop was filled with ticking timepieces, each keeping a different rhythm, yet Elias's life seemed to move in slow motion.

One rainy afternoon, a young girl named Maya burst in, clutching a broken music box that had belonged to her late grandmother. "It used to play the song of the sea," she whispered, "but now it's just silence."

Elias took the box gently. Inside, the gears were tangled, not broken. He spent hours untangling them, humming softly as he worked. When he finally wound the key, the music box didn't just play a tune; it played the sound of crashing waves and seagulls, filling the dusty shop with life
